cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AEON in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "AEON: from raw SPHEREx frames to the age, mass and orbit of what moves in the infrared sky"
abstract: >-
  AEON is an open-source pipeline and web observatory for NASA's SPHEREx all-sky survey,
  built for the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026 ("Planet X and SPHEREx"). It reduces real
  SPHEREx Level-2 spectral images to 102-band near-infrared spectra, combines each spectrum
  with the object's Galactic kinematics to estimate its age and mass against published
  evolution models, integrates past and future orbits (galpy for stars and brown dwarfs,
  REBOUND for solar-system candidates), and validates every result against SIMBAD and the
  peer-reviewed literature.
authors:
  - name: "Team AEON"
repository-code: "https://github.com/alpztel/aeon"
url: "https://github.com/alpztel/aeon"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-15"
keywords:
  - SPHEREx
  - Planet X
  - brown dwarfs
  - stellar kinematics
  - galactic dynamics
  - astronomy
  - NASA Space Apps Challenge
